  "facets": [
    {
      "title": "Localization-Friendly Writing",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "Reference for writing source-language strings that translate cleanly into 30+ locales.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/localization-friendly-writing/#localization-friendly-writing",
          "note": null,
          "level": 0
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "The one rule: write so a translator can reorder, expand, and replace",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "Every translation operation needs three freedoms:",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/localization-friendly-writing/#the-one-rule-write-so-a-translator-can-reorder-expand-and-replace",
          "note": null,
          "level": 0
        },
        {
          "text": "Reorder - subject-verb-object in English is not subject-verb-object in Japanese or German.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/localization-friendly-writing/#the-one-rule-write-so-a-translator-can-reorder-expand-and-replace",
          "note": null,
          "level": 1
        },
        {
          "text": "Expand - German, Russian, Finnish run 30–40% longer than English.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/localization-friendly-writing/#the-one-rule-write-so-a-translator-can-reorder-expand-and-replace",
          "note": null,
          "level": 1
        },
        {
          "text": "Replace - Plural forms, gendered forms, formal/informal address.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/localization-friendly-writing/#the-one-rule-write-so-a-translator-can-reorder-expand-and-replace",
          "note": null,
          "level": 1
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Core concept 1 — The translation-friendly English rules",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "One sentence, one idea. Compound sentences with subordinate clauses become unparseable in OV languages.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/localization-friendly-writing/#core-concept-1-the-translation-friendly-english-rules",
          "note": null,
          "level": 0
        },
        {
          "text": "Subject-verb-object, in that order.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/localization-friendly-writing/#core-concept-1-the-translation-friendly-english-rules",
          "note": null,
          "level": 0
        },
        {
          "text": "No idioms. \"Hit the ground running\" has no German equivalent.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/localization-friendly-writing/#core-concept-1-the-translation-friendly-english-rules",
          "note": null,
          "level": 0
        },
        {
          "text": "No metaphors. \"Move the needle\" requires a needle, which requires a gauge, which requires the metaphor to land.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/localization-friendly-writing/#core-concept-1-the-translation-friendly-english-rules",
          "note": null,
          "level": 0
        },
        {
          "text": "No cultural references. No baseball, no Thanksgiving, no Marvel cinematic universe.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/localization-friendly-writing/#core-concept-1-the-translation-friendly-english-rules",
          "note": null,
          "level": 0
        },
        {
          "text": "Avoid humour and wordplay. Puns are untranslatable by definition.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/localization-friendly-writing/#core-concept-1-the-translation-friendly-english-rules",
          "note": null,
          "level": 0
        },
        {
          "text": "No abbreviations the reader must decode. \"Q1,\" \"EOY,\" \"ASAP\" - spell them out at first use.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/localization-friendly-writing/#core-concept-1-the-translation-friendly-english-rules",
          "note": null,
          "level": 0
        },
        {
          "text": "No phrasal verbs where a single verb works. \"Set up the account\" becomes \"create the account.\"",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/localization-friendly-writing/#core-concept-1-the-translation-friendly-english-rules",
          "note": null,
          "level": 0
        },
        {
          "text": "No latinate jargon. \"Utilize\" → \"use.\" \"Initiate\" → \"start.\"",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/localization-friendly-writing/#core-concept-1-the-translation-friendly-english-rules",
          "note": null,
          "level": 0
        },
        {
          "text": "Active voice as the default.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/localization-friendly-writing/#core-concept-1-the-translation-friendly-english-rules",
          "note": null,
          "level": 0
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Core concept 2 — ICU MessageFormat: plural",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "Common mistake - only English plural categories:",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/localization-friendly-writing/#core-concept-2-icu-messageformat-plural",
          "note": null,
          "level": 0
        },
        {
          "text": "This works for English. It silently breaks Russian, Polish, Arabic.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/localization-friendly-writing/#core-concept-2-icu-messageformat-plural",
          "note": null,
          "level": 0
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Core concept 3 — CLDR plural categories",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "other is required. Every plural block must include other.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/localization-friendly-writing/#core-concept-3-cldr-plural-categories",
          "note": null,
          "level": 0
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Core concept 4 — ICU select and selectordinal",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "select is a switch over a string variable, typically used for gender:",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/localization-friendly-writing/#core-concept-4-icu-select-and-selectordinal",
          "note": null,
          "level": 0
        },
        {
          "text": "other is required even in select.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/localization-friendly-writing/#core-concept-4-icu-select-and-selectordinal",
          "note": null,
          "level": 0
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Core concept 5 — Placeholders that survive translation",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "Use named placeholders, not positional. {username} survives word reorder. %s %s does not.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/localization-friendly-writing/#core-concept-5-placeholders-that-survive-translation",
          "note": null,
          "level": 1
        },
        {
          "text": "Never concatenate. \"Hello, \" + username + \"!\" forces English word order.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/localization-friendly-writing/#core-concept-5-placeholders-that-survive-translation",
          "note": null,
          "level": 1
        },
        {
          "text": "Always provide a comment describing the placeholder.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/localization-friendly-writing/#core-concept-5-placeholders-that-survive-translation",
          "note": null,
          "level": 1
        },
        {
          "text": "Concatenation anti-pattern:",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/localization-friendly-writing/#core-concept-5-placeholders-that-survive-translation",
          "note": null,
          "level": 0
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Core concept 6 — Translator comments",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "Every non-trivial string gets a translator comment answering:",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/localization-friendly-writing/#core-concept-6-translator-comments",
          "note": null,
          "level": 0
        },
        {
          "text": "What is this? UI element type (button, error, tooltip, heading).",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/localization-friendly-writing/#core-concept-6-translator-comments",
          "note": null,
          "level": 1
        },
        {
          "text": "What does the placeholder mean? {count} = unread messages, integer ≥ 0.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/localization-friendly-writing/#core-concept-6-translator-comments",
          "note": null,
          "level": 1
        },
        {
          "text": "Where does it appear?",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/localization-friendly-writing/#core-concept-6-translator-comments",
          "note": null,
          "level": 1
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Core concept 7 — Pseudo-localization",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "Pseudo-localization is a smoke test that runs before any human translator sees the strings. It:",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/localization-friendly-writing/#core-concept-7-pseudo-localization",
          "note": null,
          "level": 0
        },
        {
          "text": "Expands every string 30–40% to surface truncation bugs",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/localization-friendly-writing/#core-concept-7-pseudo-localization",
          "note": null,
          "level": 1
        },
        {
          "text": "Replaces ASCII characters with accented Latin equivalents",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/localization-friendly-writing/#core-concept-7-pseudo-localization",
          "note": null,
          "level": 1
        },
        {
          "text": "Wraps every string with sentinels like [!! … !!] to surface un-extracted strings",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/localization-friendly-writing/#core-concept-7-pseudo-localization",
          "note": null,
          "level": 1
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Core concept 8 — RTL-friendly writing",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "Avoid baked-in directional assumptions. \"Click the arrow on the right\" becomes wrong in Arabic. Prefer \"Click the arrow next to the search box.\"",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/localization-friendly-writing/#core-concept-8-rtl-friendly-writing",
          "note": null,
          "level": 0
        },
        {
          "text": "Numbers stay LTR inside RTL text. This is automatic in Unicode bidi.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/localization-friendly-writing/#core-concept-8-rtl-friendly-writing",
          "note": null,
          "level": 0
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Core concept 10 — Key naming conventions",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "The key describes the role, not the content.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/localization-friendly-writing/#core-concept-10-key-naming-conventions",
          "note": null,
          "level": 0
        },
        {
          "text": "Namespace by feature, then by sub-feature.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/localization-friendly-writing/#core-concept-10-key-naming-conventions",
          "note": null,
          "level": 0
        },
        {
          "text": "Don't bury locale in the key.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/localization-friendly-writing/#core-concept-10-key-naming-conventions",
          "note": null,
          "level": 0
        }
      ]
    },
